# No JSON blocks in the Quinovo frontend

The Quinovo frontend must **never** display raw JSON to users. Anywhere.
Landing page, workspace chrome, graph inspector, object view, catalog,
inference, audit, settings, train, connect, sources, SDK — all of it.

## What "raw JSON" means

Any of these, rendered into served HTML, is a violation:

- `<details class="json-panel">` / `<pre>` JSON dumps
- `<pre><code>{ ... }</code></pre>` config blocks
- `JSON.stringify(obj, null, 2)` shown on the page
- A `<pre>` block whose contents are JSON / YAML / a config object
- A `json_panel(...)` / `jsonPanel(...)` call that emits visible JSON

## What to do instead

- Show **human language**. Use the helpers in `quinovo/apps/humanize.py`
  (`title_case`, `fact_line`, `status_label`, `confidence_label`, …) to turn
  kernel data into sentences.
- For agent connection, show **agent logo cards**
  (`quinovo/apps/agents.py`) — logo, name, one-line blurb, and plain-language
  steps. The launch command is a **single line** in a styled `<input>`
  (`.agent-cmd`), never a JSON block.
- If a power user needs the raw config, the **Copy config** button fetches it
  from `/connect/config/{agent}` (plain text) and puts it on the clipboard.
  The raw config is **never rendered** on the page. Link to the API endpoint
  (e.g. `/contract.json`) instead of dumping it inline.
- `quinovo/apps/chrome.py::json_panel` is a **no-op** that returns `""`.
  Do not call it. Do not reintroduce it. If you need a "view source"
  affordance, link to the JSON API endpoint — do not render a `<pre>`.

## Enforcement

- Grep rendered pages before finishing: no `json-panel`, no `jsonPanel`,
  no `<pre`, no `cfg-code`, no `cfg-toggle`/`cfg-grid` JSON dumps.
- Tests in `tests/test_*.py` assert `"json-panel" not in page.text` and
  `"<pre" not in page.text` for every served page. Keep them green and add
  the same assertion to any new page test.
- Human-language UI is codified in `skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md`.
  Layout, graphics, and motion are in
  `.cursor/skills/databricks-visual-language/SKILL.md`.
  Read both before touching any file under `src/quinovo/apps/`.

## Why

Quinovo is human-first. The loop runs itself; humans only approve. Showing
raw JSON to an approver is a bug, not a feature. Power users have the API
and the copy button — the page itself stays clean.
